From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:23:31 +0930
Subject: [PATCH 11/24] spiFlashdb: consistent manufacturer capitalisation

"micron", "spansion" and "microchip" were lower case while every other
manufacturer (Macronix, Winbond, ISSI, ...) is capitalised, so the
"Detected:" line and --flash-info spelled vendors inconsistently. The
string is only displayed, never compared.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F2L6L5SJYvbBUUt4DinjGC
---
 doc/guide/advanced.rst |  2 +-
 src/spiFlashdb.hpp     | 34 +++++++++++++++++-----------------
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/guide/advanced.rst b/doc/guide/advanced.rst
index b6e5066..70d2dfc 100644
